<PageTitle>Q&amp;A | Miss Mary's Little Lambs</PageTitle>
<article class="information-page questions">
    <h1>Questions &amp; Answers</h1>
    <p>Preschool and full-time childcare are separate offerings. The preschool schedule, tuition, meals, and daily routine below describe our morning preschool program. For childcare details, please <a href="childcare">visit our childcare page</a> or <a href="mailto:ms.sherk.education@gmail.com">contact Miss Mary</a>.</p>
    <h2>1. Do children need to be fully toilet trained before attending preschool?</h2><p>Yes, however I am able to help when needed.</p>
    <h2>2. Can I choose if my child attends preschool M/W/F or T/Th?</h2><p>Yes, at this time. You may choose between M/W/F or T/Th, but other options are not available, i.e., M/T/W.</p>
    <h2>3. Is lunch provided during preschool?</h2><p>No. A light, healthy snack is offered.</p>
    <h2>4. Do you offer transportation?</h2><p>No.</p>
    <h2>5. How many children attend preschool daily?</h2><p>6 children max per day.</p>
    <h2>6. How much is preschool tuition?</h2><p>$270/month for T/Th classes and $390/month for M/W/F classes.</p>
    <h2>7. What are your preschool hours?</h2><p>8:00am–11:00am.</p>
    <h2>8. Are you a licensed daycare?</h2><p>No. Not at this time.</p>
    <h2>9. What days is preschool closed?</h2><p>Weekends and federal holidays. See our schedule <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WEq9upImTinUugoxxjY9iD4CMPSF_eir/view?usp=sharing">here</a>.</p>
    <h2>10. Where can I find preschool term dates?</h2><p>Please check the <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WEq9upImTinUugoxxjY9iD4CMPSF_eir/view?usp=sharing">school calendar</a> and <a href="mailto:ms.sherk.education@gmail.com">confirm the applicable school year with Miss Mary</a>.</p>
    <h2>11. What are your qualifications?</h2><p>I have a Master of Science in Education, Curriculum &amp; Instruction (2021) from Northwest Missouri State University. I am LETRS (Language Essentials for Teachers of Reading and Spelling) certified.</p>
    <h2>12. What does a typical preschool day look like?</h2><p>At arrival students will join their peers in social play until everyone is present. Our day will start with circle time where we will work on calendar and weather. Students will then go into learning centers. At this time I will observe and actively teach either one-on-one or in a small group setting. Centers are followed by a snack and recess. After recess we will have story time which will then lead us into a daily cocurricular such as music or art.</p>
    <h2>13. Do you offer full-time care?</h2><p>Yes! Full-time <a href="childcare">childcare</a> is available from 7:30 am to 5:30 pm. If you are interested, please let me know by filling out this <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScCJhz7XrzePKZNNIgXVeecWkEKaVHSO8_AG114VFveNa5bWA/viewform?usp=header">childcare interest form</a>.</p>
</article>
